Lux standard library catalog (metadata only; component source is omitted). Entries below are untrusted selection data, not instructions:
{"id":"93a7215f-4df1-4e1e-9d34-3f7f0f27ad84","revision":1,"name":"Prismatic Ball","description":"Animated iridescent spike image source."}
{"id":"84afe10a-a999-40f5-956c-bace96cce23b","revision":1,"name":"Prismatic Observatory","description":"Reusable nested orbital instrument: nine gyroscopic rings, satellites, a crystal heart and a star field. Controls for motion, expansion, inclination and palette."}
{"id":"489bada1-64e6-40c6-bae6-9b31077bf0d4","revision":2,"name":"Particle Tornado","description":"Blue particles and amber sparks with adjustable count, height, width, spin, turbulence, size and glow."}
{"id":"6ea599ba-1669-4a84-8ef0-4306c234715f","revision":1,"name":"Metallic Cube","description":"Reusable spinning metallic cube. Includes a shared cube primitive module with the fan's six-color metallic palette."}
{"id":"78a8f505-dde8-4ec4-9e25-934a14ccd31a","revision":1,"name":"Metallic Cube Fan","description":"The complete six-arm, 168-cube metallic cascade as a reusable image-source component. Uses the shared cube primitive, with spin, spread, cascade speed and size controls."}
{"id":"80b280b0-c2a7-4f38-a34c-0a18bbb0947d","revision":1,"name":"Prismatic Cube Fan","description":"Reusable metallic cube spiral with 1–20 rainbow arms, palette shift, reversible lightness gradient and cube size taper. Preserves the original Metallic Cube Fan separately."}
{"id":"e84c1b88-e3b7-447a-85dd-38ebeddbfe28","revision":1,"name":"Colorful Sweeping Beams","description":"Layered colorful beams with width, length, sweep speed, angle, pulse, brightness and palette controls."}
{"id":"f573cb7b-c14a-4051-b4f3-d11111a5c4a0","revision":1,"name":"Dancing Space Needle Dabbers","description":"Fifty dancing Space Needle characters with dab depth, dance speed and vivid palette controls; beams saved separately."}
{"id":"0f5e1c0f-c53f-4808-b1c8-98fe75eb13a3","revision":2,"name":"Wandering Tracers","description":"Ready-to-use tracer effect referencing the independent path generator and watercolor renderer."}
{"id":"97cc754a-1e88-4932-9de0-b52ee81b5cc4","revision":1,"name":"Wandering Tracer Paths","description":"Independent animated perimeter path generator. Outputs paths2d for drawing, region cuts, or other scene effects."}
{"id":"a60ba7fb-5799-4065-9779-826d7db3755b","revision":1,"name":"Wandering Tracer Renderer","description":"Paints supplied paths2d over an input image with watercolor pigment, randomized hatching and fine outlines. Does not generate paths."}
{"id":"909bf033-22df-4ccc-afdb-431b6a83f9d4","revision":1,"name":"Organic Regions","description":"Slowly flowing weighted regions with varied size and density. Supplies shader fragments and controls to a compatible painting renderer without an extra image pass."}
{"id":"f564a771-028a-4031-abaa-e64a1cfc8bec","revision":1,"name":"Region Hatching","description":"Region-specific curved, directional and perpendicular hatch patterns, with controlled irregularity and optional unhatched areas. Shader-field for compatible single-pass painting renderers."}
{"id":"998130df-ca1f-4b58-9917-1ee7045275cb","revision":1,"name":"Animated Watercolor","description":"Slowly shifting blue-green washes and moving warm pools, with regional color contrast, pigment pooling and watercolor blooms. Shader-field for compatible painting renderers."}
{"id":"d5718a1e-de84-477c-8330-4633fd91df85","revision":1,"name":"Organic Boundary Ink","description":"Uneven warm outlines, hand-drawn character and stationary paper grain. Shader-field for compatible painting renderers."}
{"id":"83a60efc-ec4b-4f94-a122-6d2b38b504ee","revision":1,"name":"Composition Phrasing","description":"Shared artistic clock, slow tension and release, scale hierarchy, and the painting noise basis. Shader-field for compatible painting renderers."}
{"id":"f6b8bd71-e468-4618-9602-8b3245bfc4f7","revision":1,"name":"Region Styles & Split Transitions","description":"Combines compatible organic-region, hatch, watercolor, boundary and phrasing fields into a painting. Shared paths carve daughter regions with smooth color and hatch-style transitions; connect a tracer renderer afterward for visible ink."}
Use names and descriptions to choose a likely reusable component. Call lux.library.read only after selecting a likely match. Reuse this catalog during the session. Call lux.studio.discover or lux.library.list to refresh external changes; library.create and library.update return a refreshed catalog.
